From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:47:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] replay: mark the begin-record start snapshot; refuse loads
 while recording

x-rr-begin-record reloads its start snapshot and records from the loaded
state, so replay_load_snapshot() (0140) turns the timers due at the loaded
clock into vCPU work on every load of it.  The start snapshot now carries a
"replay/begin" subsection of the "replay" section, saved only by
x-rr-begin-record's save_snapshot, and a load of a snapshot so marked
converts (the name rule stays for start snapshots saved before the mark).
The log's format is unchanged.

Such a recording replayed in a fresh process with -icount
rr=replay,rrfile=,rrsnapshot= cannot work: its log has nothing of machine
init, nor of the snapshot load's block requests (x-rr-begin-record saved and
reloaded with the events off, before replay_start(), as x-rr-begin-replay
loads), and the network filters x-rr-begin-record added are not on the
command line.  On x86 the load hung for ever in blkreplay's flush of the
vmstate (with the events switched off for the load, it then failed an
assertion in bdrv_drain_all_end), before the timers mattered.  The startup
load now stops at the mark with an error that says to replay with
x-rr-begin-replay; boards that draw random data at machine init (virt's fdt
rng-seed) stop earlier, and "Missing random event" now says the same.

load_snapshot() was not refused under record/replay (HMP/QMP loadvm,
snapshot-load, and PANDA's panda_revert / penguin_load_snapshot): the log
has no event for the load, so a recording with a revert in it could not be
replayed.  replay_can_load_snapshot() refuses every load while recording or
replaying except record/replay's own (replay_load_snapshot(): the start
snapshot and a reverse-debugging seek) and -loadvm, which runs before the
run and which a replay given the same command line repeats.  loadvm and
snapshot-load check before stopping the VM, so a refused load leaves it
running.  A savevm that would replace the start snapshot while recording or
replaying is refused too (its replay loads that snapshot).

The stall check's deadline recomputation is deliberate (the caller's was
taken before the timers ran): say so.
